; core-word-ack.fk — from the core words to an ack whose node-id is worn
; only as wide as the moment needs.
;
; offer-ack-core.fk answers WHICH arm an offer is acknowledged by
; ({nothing, 0, 1, node}, axiom-5). It says nothing about HOW WIDE the node
; arm has to be. That is the gap this cell fills: a node-ack carries an
; identity, an identity has a width, and the width is not a constant — it is
; decided, per query, by how much the asker and the answerer already share.
;
; GROUND
;   axiom-1 states       — 0, 1, nothing; nothing is the ground, and no answer
;                          in the time given IS nothing, never an error.
;   axiom-2 cell         — a cell is four integers (pkg level type inst). The
;                          core words are cells; nothing here is metaphor.
;   axiom-3 addressing   — identity is the present composition. Two spellings
;                          that differ in case are two compositions, so two
;                          cells — "we" and "We" are not one word twice.
;   axiom-4 boundary     — the cell decides what it offers and what it trusts.
;                          The width below is decided by the answering cell
;                          against its own held original; no outside authority
;                          grants it. That is the whole of "trusted by inner
;                          knowing" — a check the speaker can run on itself.
;   axiom-5 offer        — the four acks. Built here through oac-*, never
;                          re-shaped.
;
; THE THREE LAYERS, IN ORDER
;
;   1. THE CORE WORDS. Sixteen: nothing 0 1 | I you me we us | do be exist |
;      when where what how why. Each is a cell at (1, family, polarity, index).
;      pkg is 1 for all of them — see the finding below.
;
;   2. THE QUERY, LAYERED ON TOP. (subject verb qword fuel point): a subject
;      word, a verb from {do, be, exist}, a question word from
;      {when where what how why}, the fuel the moment allows, and the point
;      it is asked from — itself a core word, because a standpoint is a cell.
;
;   3. THE ACK. Exactly one of nothing / 0 / 1 / node. The verb picks the arm
;      family (be/exist ask a state, do asks an identity); the CASE of the
;      question word picks the scope; the scope picks the width.
;
; CLUSIVITY — THE CASE IS NOT DECORATION
;   Lower case is exclusive by default, upper case inclusive by default. This
;   is not a convention invented here: it is clusivity, the distinction many
;   languages mark in the first person plural and English does not — the
;   "we" that leaves the listener out against the "we" that takes them in
;   (Indonesian kami / kita, three streets from where this was written).
;   English writes it nowhere, so the case slot is free to carry it.
;
;   And the case slot carries the width, because the two are the same fact:
;   an exclusive question narrows the field it stays unique against, so the
;   answer can be short; an inclusive question widens it, so the same answer
;   is worn longer. Openness is paid for in identity.
;
;   One asymmetry falls out and is checked below rather than asserted: an
;   inclusive existence question cannot be answered "no". Its scope is the
;   whole field, so every core word is in it. Only the exclusive question has
;   the power to return 0. To be able to hear no, ask exclusively.
;
;   One word in the table has no lower-case form: English writes no "i".
;   The first person singular has no exclusive spelling, which is right —
;   I cannot exclude myself from myself. The table does not add one, and the
;   band checks that "i" is not a core word while "I" is.
;
; THE COMPRESSION, AND WHAT IT COSTS
;   A NodeID is not a hash. Its leading coordinates are the shared context and
;   its trailing coordinates are what discriminates — the opposite end from a
;   git prefix. So "as compressed as possible" means dropping coordinates from
;   the FRONT, and the dropped slots come back zeroed:
;
;     width 4  (pkg level type inst)   nothing dropped
;     width 3  (0   level type inst)   pkg borrowed from the point
;     width 2  (0   0     type inst)
;     width 1  (0   0     0    inst)
;     width 0  (0   0     0    0   )   no identity at all
;
;   Width 0 is not a degenerate case, it is the best answer: when the scope
;   holds exactly one cell, the question already singled it out and the node
;   arm collapses to the terminal 1. Asking well costs the answer nothing.
;
;   The debt: a compressed id is expanded by taking the missing leading
;   coordinates FROM THE POINT. If the point does not carry them, expansion
;   does not fail — it lands on a different, perfectly valid cell. Silent
;   misidentification, not an error. (The kernel has been bitten by exactly
;   this shape once already: bp's old fallback collapsed every unregistered
;   name onto one NodeID, and distinct blueprints collided invisibly.) So
;   cwa-trusted? is checked before any node arm is handed back, and a point
;   that cannot carry the prefix gets nothing instead of a wrong node.
;
;   The asymmetry worth naming: only the SPEAKER can run that check, because
;   only the speaker still holds the original. The listener cannot verify a
;   compressed id at all — it can only trust the shared standpoint. Compression
;   is a debt owed to a point of view, and it is the speaker who is good
;   for it.
;
; FINDING, MEASURED BY THE BAND, NOT ASSERTED
;   Across the whole 29-cell field, no answer ever needs width 4: pkg is 1
;   everywhere, so a quarter of every identity is pure context and free to
;   drop. And the two cells that compress FURTHEST are "0" and "1" — the
;   caseless ones. Having no case, they sit in no clusivity band, and that
;   absence is what makes them cheap to name. The two acks axiom-5 calls
;   terminal turn out to be the cheapest identities in the field.
;
; Proof: form-stdlib/tests/core-word-ack-band.fk → four-way (Go/Rust/TS/fkwu).
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk ../control/offer-ack-core.fk

(do
    ;; ── layer 1: the core words as cells ────────────────────────────
    ;; A row is (word family index); the polarity is READ off the spelling,
    ;; never restated, so the table cannot drift from the case it claims.
    (defn cwa-row (word fam idx) (list word fam idx))
    (defn cwa-word (r) (nth r 0))
    (defn cwa-fam  (r) (nth r 1))
    (defn cwa-idx  (r) (nth r 2))

    ;; case, by byte: A-Z is 65..90, a-z is 97..122. "0" and "1" are neither.
    (defn cwa-upper? (w)
        (if (gt (str_byte_at w 0) 64) (if (lt (str_byte_at w 0) 91) 1 0) 0))
    (defn cwa-lower? (w)
        (if (gt (str_byte_at w 0) 96) (if (lt (str_byte_at w 0) 123) 1 0) 0))
    ;; 2 = inclusive (upper), 1 = exclusive (lower), 0 = caseless (no band)
    (defn cwa-polarity (w)
        (if (eq (cwa-upper? w) 1) 2 (if (eq (cwa-lower? w) 1) 1 0)))
    (defn cwa-pol (r) (cwa-polarity (cwa-word r)))

    ;; ── the spacing: numeric distance IS distance-to-root ───────────
    ;; Urs: the numeric space should be spaced so that coordinates near the
    ;; ROOT sit far apart and details near the LEAF sit close together —
    ;; details closer together than stark difference.
    ;;
    ;; Dense ordinals (family 1..4, polarity 0..2, index 0..4) cannot do this:
    ;; a family change and an index change both read as "1", so the number
    ;; carries no depth. Giving each coordinate a stride that grows with its
    ;; nearness to the root makes the arithmetic difference say WHERE two
    ;; cells diverge, not merely THAT they do:
    ;;
    ;;   family (nearest the root)  stride 1000
    ;;   polarity (the clusivity)   stride  100
    ;;   index (the leaf detail)    stride    1
    ;;
    ;;   |we - us|  =    1   two persons, same clusivity — a detail
    ;;   |we - We|  =  100   the clusivity flips — one level up
    ;;   |we - why| = 2001   a different family — stark
    ;;
    ;; This is the same fact as the compression, seen from the other side.
    ;; Truncating an id drops its LEADING coordinates, which are exactly the
    ;; widest strides — so a short id is the fine detail with the stark
    ;; differences borrowed from the point. Numeric nearness and cheap
    ;; identity are one property, and cwa-metric-sound? below proves the
    ;; divergence depth of ANY pair is readable from |difference| alone.
    (defn cwa-fam-stride () 1000)
    (defn cwa-pol-stride ()  100)
    (defn cwa-idx-stride ()    1)

    ;; the widest spread each coordinate can contribute
    (defn cwa-idx-span () 4)                              ; families run 0..4
    (defn cwa-pol-span () (mul (cwa-pol-stride) 2))       ; polarity runs 0..2
    ;; two cells of one family+polarity never differ by more than this
    (defn cwa-same-band-max () (cwa-idx-span))
    ;; two cells of one family never differ by more than this
    (defn cwa-same-fam-max () (add (cwa-pol-span) (cwa-idx-span)))

    ;; The space is a metric only while a family step outruns everything
    ;; below it. Stated as a guard, not a hope: add a 300th word or a sixth
    ;; index and this goes 0 rather than the band staying quietly green.
    (defn cwa-strides-sound? ()
        (if (gt (sub (cwa-fam-stride) (cwa-same-fam-max)) (cwa-same-fam-max)) 1 0))

    ;; the cell: pkg is 1 for every core word — one package, hence never a
    ;; discriminator, hence always droppable. level/type carry the SPACED
    ;; values, so the coordinates themselves hold the depth.
    (defn cwa-pkg () 1)
    (defn cwa-level (r) (mul (cwa-fam r) (cwa-fam-stride)))
    (defn cwa-type  (r) (mul (cwa-pol r) (cwa-pol-stride)))
    (defn cwa-inst  (r) (mul (cwa-idx r) (cwa-idx-stride)))
    (defn cwa-nid (r) (make_nodeid (cwa-pkg) (cwa-level r) (cwa-type r) (cwa-inst r)))

    ;; the scalar address — the three spaced coordinates summed. The strides
    ;; do not overlap, so the sum is injective and |a - b| is a true distance.
    (defn cwa-address (r) (add (cwa-level r) (add (cwa-type r) (cwa-inst r))))
    (defn cwa-abs (x) (if (lt x 0) (sub 0 x) x))
    (defn cwa-dist (a b) (cwa-abs (sub (cwa-address a) (cwa-address b))))

    ;; the depth at which two cells actually diverge:
    ;;   2 = different family (stark)  1 = clusivity flip  0 = same band, a detail
    (defn cwa-depth-actual (a b)
        (if (eq (cwa-fam a) (cwa-fam b))
            (if (eq (cwa-pol a) (cwa-pol b)) 0 1)
            2))
    ;; the same depth, read from the DISTANCE alone — no access to the cells
    (defn cwa-depth-from-dist (d)
        (if (le d (cwa-same-band-max)) 0
            (if (le d (cwa-same-fam-max)) 1 2)))

    ;; families: 1 states, 2 persons, 3 verbs, 4 questions
    (defn cwa-field ()
        (list
            ; the three states (axiom-1). "0" and "1" carry no case at all.
            (cwa-row "nothing" 1 0) (cwa-row "Nothing" 1 0)
            (cwa-row "0"       1 1) (cwa-row "1"       1 2)
            ; the persons. No lower-case "I": the first person has no
            ; exclusive spelling in English, and needs none.
            (cwa-row "I"   2 0)
            (cwa-row "you" 2 1) (cwa-row "You" 2 1)
            (cwa-row "me"  2 2) (cwa-row "Me"  2 2)
            (cwa-row "we"  2 3) (cwa-row "We"  2 3)
            (cwa-row "us"  2 4) (cwa-row "Us"  2 4)
            ; the verbs
            (cwa-row "do"    3 0) (cwa-row "Do"    3 0)
            (cwa-row "be"    3 1) (cwa-row "Be"    3 1)
            (cwa-row "exist" 3 2) (cwa-row "Exist" 3 2)
            ; the questions
            (cwa-row "when"  4 0) (cwa-row "When"  4 0)
            (cwa-row "where" 4 1) (cwa-row "Where" 4 1)
            (cwa-row "what"  4 2) (cwa-row "What"  4 2)
            (cwa-row "how"   4 3) (cwa-row "How"   4 3)
            (cwa-row "why"   4 4) (cwa-row "Why"   4 4)))

    (defn cwa-find-loop (rs w)
        (if (eq (len rs) 0) (list)
            (if (str_eq (cwa-word (head rs)) w) (head rs)
                (cwa-find-loop (tail rs) w))))
    (defn cwa-find (w) (cwa-find-loop (cwa-field) w))
    (defn cwa-known? (w) (if (eq (len (cwa-find w)) 0) 0 1))
    (defn cwa-count () (len (cwa-field)))

    ;; ── the width machinery ─────────────────────────────────────────
    ;; two ids agree on their last n coordinates
    (defn cwa-suffix-eq (a b n)
        (if (eq n 0) 1
            (if (eq (node_inst a) (node_inst b))
                (if (eq n 1) 1
                    (if (eq (node_type a) (node_type b))
                        (if (eq n 2) 1
                            (if (eq (node_level a) (node_level b))
                                (if (eq n 3) 1
                                    (if (eq (node_pkg a) (node_pkg b)) 1 0))
                                0))
                        0))
                0)))

    ;; how many cells in the scope wear the same n-wide suffix
    (defn cwa-share-count (scope nid n)
        (if (eq (len scope) 0) 0
            (add (if (eq (cwa-suffix-eq (cwa-nid (head scope)) nid n) 1) 1 0)
                 (cwa-share-count (tail scope) nid n))))

    ;; the narrowest width that still points at exactly one cell of the scope.
    ;; 5 means no width names it from here — the cell is not in this scope.
    (defn cwa-width-from (scope nid n)
        (if (gt n 4) 5
            (if (eq (cwa-share-count scope nid n) 1) n
                (cwa-width-from scope nid (add n 1)))))
    (defn cwa-min-width (scope nid) (cwa-width-from scope nid 0))

    ;; drop the leading coordinates; the dropped slots come back zeroed
    (defn cwa-compress (nid n)
        (make_nodeid (if (ge n 4) (node_pkg   nid) 0)
                     (if (ge n 3) (node_level nid) 0)
                     (if (ge n 2) (node_type  nid) 0)
                     (if (ge n 1) (node_inst  nid) 0)))

    ;; put them back from the point of view — the point pays what was dropped
    (defn cwa-expand (point short n)
        (make_nodeid (if (ge n 4) (node_pkg   short) (node_pkg   point))
                     (if (ge n 3) (node_level short) (node_level point))
                     (if (ge n 2) (node_type  short) (node_type  point))
                     (if (ge n 1) (node_inst  short) (node_inst  point))))

    ;; inner knowing: the speaker checks the round trip against the original
    ;; it still holds. Nobody grants this; nobody else can run it.
    (defn cwa-trusted? (point nid n)
        (if (node_eq (cwa-expand point (cwa-compress nid n) n) nid) 1 0))

    ;; ── layer 2: the query ──────────────────────────────────────────
    (defn cwa-query (subject verb qword fuel point)
        (list subject verb qword fuel point))
    (defn cwa-q-subject (q) (nth q 0))
    (defn cwa-q-verb    (q) (nth q 1))
    (defn cwa-q-word    (q) (nth q 2))
    (defn cwa-q-fuel    (q) (nth q 3))
    (defn cwa-q-point   (q) (nth q 4))

    ;; the invitation's case decides the scope — the asker's openness, not
    ;; the subject's
    (defn cwa-q-inclusive? (q) (if (eq (cwa-polarity (cwa-q-word q)) 2) 1 0))

    ;; the exclusive band of a standpoint: its own family, its own polarity
    (defn cwa-band (rs fam pol)
        (if (eq (len rs) 0) (list)
            (if (eq (cwa-fam (head rs)) fam)
                (if (eq (cwa-pol (head rs)) pol)
                    (cons (head rs) (cwa-band (tail rs) fam pol))
                    (cwa-band (tail rs) fam pol))
                (cwa-band (tail rs) fam pol))))

    ;; inclusive: the whole field. exclusive: the point's own band.
    (defn cwa-scope (prow inc)
        (if (eq inc 1) (cwa-field) (cwa-band (cwa-field) (cwa-fam prow) (cwa-pol prow))))

    (defn cwa-in-scope? (scope w)
        (if (eq (len scope) 0) 0
            (if (str_eq (cwa-word (head scope)) w) 1 (cwa-in-scope? (tail scope) w))))

    (defn cwa-verb-do? (v)
        (if (str_eq v "do") 1 (if (str_eq v "Do") 1 0)))
    (defn cwa-verb-state? (v)
        (if (str_eq v "be") 1 (if (str_eq v "Be") 1
            (if (str_eq v "exist") 1 (if (str_eq v "Exist") 1 0)))))

    ;; the width this query's answer is worn at — 5 when no width names it
    (defn cwa-width (q)
        (if (eq (cwa-known? (cwa-q-subject q)) 0) 5
            (if (eq (cwa-known? (cwa-q-point q)) 0) 5
                (cwa-min-width
                    (cwa-scope (cwa-find (cwa-q-point q)) (cwa-q-inclusive? q))
                    (cwa-nid (cwa-find (cwa-q-subject q)))))))

    ;; ── layer 3: the ack — exactly one of nothing / 0 / 1 / node ────
    ;;   no ground for the subject or the point   → nothing (never a false 0)
    ;;   be / exist, in scope                     → 1
    ;;   be / exist, out of scope                 → 0   (a real no)
    ;;   do, scope of one                         → 1   (no identity needed)
    ;;   do, width within the fuel and carried    → node, compressed
    ;;   do, more width than the moment allows    → nothing (timeout is nothing)
    ;;   do, a point that cannot carry the prefix → nothing (never a wrong node)
    (defn cwa-ack-do (q nid width)
        (if (eq width 0) (oac-one nid)
            (if (gt width (cwa-q-fuel q)) (oac-nothing)
                (if (eq (cwa-trusted? (cwa-nid (cwa-find (cwa-q-point q))) nid width) 1)
                    (oac-node (cwa-compress nid width))
                    (oac-nothing)))))

    (defn cwa-ack (q)
        (if (eq (cwa-known? (cwa-q-subject q)) 0) (oac-nothing)
            (if (eq (cwa-known? (cwa-q-point q)) 0) (oac-nothing)
                (if (eq (cwa-verb-state? (cwa-q-verb q)) 1)
                    (if (eq (cwa-in-scope?
                                (cwa-scope (cwa-find (cwa-q-point q)) (cwa-q-inclusive? q))
                                (cwa-q-subject q)) 1)
                        (oac-one (cwa-nid (cwa-find (cwa-q-subject q))))
                        (oac-zero))
                    (if (eq (cwa-verb-do? (cwa-q-verb q)) 1)
                        (if (eq (cwa-width q) 5) (oac-nothing)
                            (cwa-ack-do q (cwa-nid (cwa-find (cwa-q-subject q))) (cwa-width q)))
                        (oac-nothing))))))

    ;; ── the field's own honesty: 29 words, 29 distinct cells ────────
    (defn cwa-nid-eq-count (rs nid)
        (if (eq (len rs) 0) 0
            (add (if (node_eq (cwa-nid (head rs)) nid) 1 0)
                 (cwa-nid-eq-count (tail rs) nid))))
    (defn cwa-dup-loop (rs all)
        (if (eq (len rs) 0) 0
            (add (if (gt (cwa-nid-eq-count all (cwa-nid (head rs))) 1) 1 0)
                 (cwa-dup-loop (tail rs) all))))
    (defn cwa-dup-count () (cwa-dup-loop (cwa-field) (cwa-field)))
    (defn cwa-ids-distinct? () (if (eq (cwa-dup-count) 0) 1 0))

    ;; ── the metric's honesty ────────────────────────────────────────
    ;; the three witness distances, which climb with depth
    (defn cwa-d-leaf ()      (cwa-dist (cwa-find "we") (cwa-find "us")))
    (defn cwa-d-clusivity () (cwa-dist (cwa-find "we") (cwa-find "We")))
    (defn cwa-d-family ()    (cwa-dist (cwa-find "we") (cwa-find "why")))
    (defn cwa-ladder-ok? ()
        (if (lt (cwa-d-leaf) (cwa-d-clusivity))
            (if (lt (cwa-d-clusivity) (cwa-d-family)) 1 0) 0))

    ;; and the universal claim: for EVERY pair of the 29, the depth at which
    ;; they diverge is recoverable from |difference| alone — the number knows
    ;; how far from the root the two parted, without looking at the cells.
    (defn cwa-pair-ok? (a b)
        (if (eq (cwa-depth-from-dist (cwa-dist a b)) (cwa-depth-actual a b)) 1 0))
    (defn cwa-pair-loop (a rs)
        (if (eq (len rs) 0) 0
            (add (if (eq (cwa-pair-ok? a (head rs)) 1) 0 1)
                 (cwa-pair-loop a (tail rs)))))
    (defn cwa-metric-loop (rs all)
        (if (eq (len rs) 0) 0
            (add (cwa-pair-loop (head rs) all)
                 (cwa-metric-loop (tail rs) all))))
    (defn cwa-metric-misreads () (cwa-metric-loop (cwa-field) (cwa-field)))
    (defn cwa-metric-sound? ()
        (if (eq (cwa-strides-sound?) 1)
            (if (eq (cwa-metric-misreads) 0) 1 0) 0))

    ;; ── the band's ten readings, folded positionally ────────────────
    ;; Every one of these is computed from the field above; none is a
    ;; restatement of a constant written into the table.
    (defn cwa-check ()
        (add (if (eq (cwa-width (cwa-query "Us" "do" "what"  4 "I")) 1) 1 0)
        (add (if (eq (cwa-width (cwa-query "Us" "do" "What"  4 "I")) 3) 10 0)
        (add (if (eq (cwa-width (cwa-query "1"  "do" "What"  4 "0")) 2) 100 0)
        (add (if (eq (oac-nothing? (cwa-ack (cwa-query "1" "do" "What" 4 "I"))) 1) 1000 0)
        (add (if (eq (oac-one?  (cwa-ack (cwa-query "nothing" "do" "what" 4 "nothing"))) 1) 10000 0)
        (add (if (eq (oac-node? (cwa-ack (cwa-query "Us" "do" "what" 4 "I"))) 1) 100000 0)
        (add (if (eq (oac-zero? (cwa-ack (cwa-query "us" "exist" "what" 4 "I"))) 1)
                 (if (eq (oac-one? (cwa-ack (cwa-query "us" "Exist" "What" 4 "I"))) 1) 1000000 0) 0)
        (add (if (eq (oac-nothing? (cwa-ack (cwa-query "gravity" "exist" "what" 4 "I"))) 1) 10000000 0)
        (add (if (eq (oac-nothing? (cwa-ack (cwa-query "Us" "do" "What" 1 "I"))) 1) 100000000 0)
        (add (if (eq (cwa-ids-distinct?) 1)
                 (if (eq (cwa-known? "i") 0)
                     (if (eq (cwa-known? "I") 1) 1000000000 0) 0) 0)
        (add (if (eq (cwa-ladder-ok?) 1) 10000000000 0)
        (add (if (eq (cwa-metric-sound?) 1) 100000000000 0)
             0)))))))))))))

    0)
